<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lalitagiri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lalitagiri is a Buddhist site in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuttack">Cuttack</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, one of the 'Diamond Triangle' with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri">Ratnagiri</a> and Udayagiri. Occupied from about the 1st century BCE to the 13th century CE, it has the remains of monasteries, a large stupa in which relic caskets were found, and many sculptures of the Buddha and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bodhisattva">bodhisattvas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lalitagiri.jpg" alt="Lalitagiri" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rajani3737 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahastupha_at_Lalitgiri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
